<title>GREECE: Greece to issue 2-yr zeroes at 9.9pct May 2- min.</title>
<headline>Greece to issue 2-yr zeroes at 9.9pct May 2- min.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece will issue two-year, zero-coupon notes paying 9.9 percent May 2, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>Interest earned on the notes will be taxed at 7.5 percent upon maturity.</p>
<p>&quot;These securities are available to the entire investment public but mainly to retail investors who may replace their T-bills with similar paper of a longer maturity,&quot; the ministry said.</p>
<p>Moreover, holders of T-bills which mature May 2 may renew them at the following rates:</p>
<p>Three-month T-bills at 9.20 percent</p>
<p>Six-month T-bills at 9.50 percent</p>
<p>12-month T-bills at 10.30 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
